{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888568,"nonce":"Hcu+CZLHtSTecvFFuJnFHZDfni0=","title":"No Incident exists in the backend: there is no table, no domain type, no endpoint and no page to show one","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0052 §1–§4 define an Incident as a set of one or more Cases, drawn by a Correlator or a human, whose active/quiet state is read off its Cases, and a Case belongs to **at most one** Incident (§4, committed `69644bc`, flagged for owner review). Nothing implements it.\n\n**The demonstration.** `ls db/migrations | tail -1` is `00082_…`; no migration mentions `incident`. `web/src/routes/` has `cases.tsx` and `case-detail.tsx` and no incident route.\n\n**Why it matters.** Tracer bullet every other 0052 slice hangs off: the Correlator, the outbound subject and the Incident conversation all need an Incident to exist.\n\n**Where.** New migration: `incidents` (org, human-facing `number` like `alert_cases.number` from `00081`, drawn-by as Correlator id XOR actor) and a membership table with added_by/removed_by actor metadata and a removed tombstone, plus a **partial unique index on the Case over active (non-removed) memberships** so the at-most-one rule is enforced by the database, not by a service check; a domain package per ADR 0002's layout; endpoints in `api/openapi/openapi.yaml` — create from Case ids, add Case, remove Case, **move** Case (one transaction: remove from the old Incident, add to the new, both actors recorded), list, get; `/incidents` and `/incidents/{number}` pages; an `AlertEvent` annotation on each member Case's timeline (\"added to Incident #N by alice\", \"moved from #N to #M\").\n\n**Scope.** medium.\n\n**Done when.** Incidents are created, listed and shown at `/incidents/{number}` via the API; active/quiet is derived (any member Case open → active) and no endpoint sets it; adding a Case already in another Incident is refused with a pointer to *move*; move is atomic and attributed; a removed Case stays recorded as removed; no column on `alerts` or `alert_cases` references an Incident; openapi, Go and UI tests cover create, add, remove, move, the uniqueness refusal and derived state; `just ci` green.\n\n**Blocked by.** `ee9f306`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}